 "title": "From Shem to Abram",
 "ref": "Genesis 11; 22",
 "compact": true,
 "col": "shem",
 "intro": [
  "The second ten generations, from Shem to Abram, mirror the ten from Adam to Noah. Lifespans shorten sharply after the flood. The line then opens into Terah's family: Abram, Nahor and Haran, and their wives and children, who will reappear in the stories of Isaac and Jacob (Rebekah, Laban, Rachel and Leah descend from Nahor).",
  "Ages are those of the Hebrew text. The Septuagint, followed by Luke 3:36, adds Cainan between Arphaxad and Shelah."
 ],
 "sources": "Hebrew names: Miqra according to the Masorah. Mishnah Avot 5:2; Genesis Rabbah 38; Rashi on Genesis 11; Seder Olam. Scholarly summary after the standard commentaries.",
